<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toda of Pamplona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 885–after 958</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Toda Aznárez, Toda of Navarre</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Toda of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a> was queen consort of Sancho I Garcés of Pamplona and regent for their son García Sánchez I. Through her network of marriages she was linked to most of the royal houses of Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and she was aunt of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a>. In 958 she travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> with her grandson, the deposed King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-i-of-leon">Sancho I of León</a>, to seek the caliph's help.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/toda-of-pamplona.jpg" alt="Toda of Pamplona" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ultrasiete · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inscripci%C3%B3n_reina_Toda.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
